# The annotations of the game image $8214-$CBE7 (tape block 4): the single source of truth for src/game/*.asm
# (kit/mkgame.py --case .). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
#
# Witness: the eight builds of case.json read_builds, counted with tools/l1count.py (the runs of an entry's or a
# label's instruction, in total and per build): c1 (power-on, the title), idle-1p (one player who never moves),
# tour-type2 (the instructions page, key type 2), tour-redefine (the keys redefined, the timer run out),
# levels-1-3, fall-death, gameover-name (a game over and the name entry), levels-1-9. "Known only from the code"
# marks what no build ran. Coordinates: x 0-255 left to right, y 0-191 from the bottom of the screen up; a
# character row H counts from the bottom too (PrintChar $9C40: H = 0 is screen row 23).

@equ $03F8 BEEP ; the ROM's BEEP: the duration and the pitch on the calculator stack
@equ $2D28 STACK_A ; the ROM's STACK-A: A onto the calculator stack
@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the display file
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen attributes
@equ $5C04 KSTATE4 ; the ROM's KSTATE+4: $FF while no key is held
@equ $5C08 LAST_K ; the ROM's last key pressed
@equ $5C3D ERR_SP 2 ; the ROM's error stack pointer: tape block 3 sets it to 1, MainLoop checks it
@equ $61A8 LiveMap 3360 ; five level maps of 672 bytes: the one in play, then one a player (1-4)
@equ $6EC8 Score 6 ; the score in play: six digits 0-9, the most significant first
@equ $6ECE PlayerScores 24 ; the four players' scores, six digits each
@equ $6EE6 EggsLeft ; the eggs left on the level in play (12 at its start)
@equ $6EE7 PlayerEggs 4 ; each player's eggs left
@equ $6EEB Level ; the level in play, from 0 (level 1)
@equ $6EEC PlayerLevels 4 ; each player's level
@equ $6EF0 PlayerLives 4 ; each player's lives (5 at the start), the one in play included
@equ $72A0 SpriteBuffer 48 ; DrawSprite's 16 rows of 3 bytes
@equ $72D8 HarryX ; Harry's x (the left of the sprite)
@equ $72D9 HarryY ; Harry's y (the top of the sprite, up from the bottom)
@equ $72DA HarryFrame ; the walk frame 0-3
@equ $72DB HarryDir ; the frame base: 0 facing right, 4 facing left, $0D climbing
@equ $72DC PassCounter ; MainLoop's pass counter: the slow tick runs when it reaches 0 (every 130 passes)
@equ $72DD CellBuffer 72 ; DrawSprite's background: 3 x 3 map cells as 24 lines of 3 bytes
@equ $7325 JumpState ; 0 on foot, 1 drifting off an edge, 2 in the air
@equ $7326 JumpDx ; the jump's x step: 1, $FF or 0
@equ $7327 JumpCount ; the delay of the next vertical step, or the drift count
@equ $7328 JumpDelay ; the passes to the next vertical step
@equ $732A JumpDy ; the vertical direction: 1 up, 0 the top, $FF down
@equ $732B ScrollDelay ; the scroller's shifts to the next character (8)
@equ $732C TextIndex ; the scroller's character index; the box colour of DrawBox
@equ $732D KeyType ; the key type: 6 type 1, 5 type 2, 3 type 3 (the bits of keys 1-3)
@equ $732E KeyTable 12 ; the key set in play: (mask, port row) for up, down, left, right, jump, jump
@equ $733A Players ; the number of players 1-4
@equ $733B Player ; the player in play 1-4
@equ $733C LiftDelay ; the slow ticks to the next lift step (2)
@equ $733D ScoreScreenAddr 2 ; where AddScore prints the score: $3FFE + 7 x player
@equ $733F BonusDigits 3 ; the bonus: three digits (then a printed 0)
@equ $7342 TimeDigits 3 ; the time: three digits
@equ $7345 BonusDelay ; the slow ticks to the next bonus step (50)
@equ $7346 TimeDelay ; the slow ticks to the next time step (10)
@equ $7347 BonusRunning ; 1 while the bonus counts down
@equ $7348 DuckX ; the duck's x
@equ $7349 DuckY ; the duck's y
@equ $734A DuckDx ; the duck's x speed -5..5
@equ $734B DuckDy ; the duck's y speed -5..5
@equ $734C DuckDelay ; the slow ticks to the next duck step (12)
@equ $734D DuckFrame ; the duck's wing frame 0-1
@equ $734E Lift1 2 ; the screen address of lift platform 1
@equ $7350 LiftX ; the lift's x ($FF: no lift)
@equ $7351 Lift1Row ; platform 1's height count 3-165
@equ $7352 Lift2 2 ; the screen address of platform 2
@equ $7354 Lift2Row ; platform 2's height count
@equ $7355 OnLift ; 1 while Harry rides a lift
@equ $7356 HenTurn ; the hen MoveHen moved last 0-4 (it adds one, wrapping, before the move)
@equ $7357 Hens 20 ; five hen records: x ($FF: none), y, state, a spare byte
@equ $736B HenDelay ; the slow ticks to the next hen move (3, 2 from level 33)
@equ $736C RandomPtr 2 ; MoveHen's pointer into the ROM's first 256 bytes; its low byte is zeroed on every level by SetupLevel's LD (HenDelay),HL at $AFB0 (HL = 1), so the hens' random sequence restarts at the same point each level
@equ $736E LastTenThousands ; the score's 10 000s digit at the last extra life check
@equ $736F TitleTuneDone ; 1 once the title tune has played
@equ $7370 SoundSweep ; the pickup sound's count ($FF after an egg or grain)
@equ $7373 PhraseTimer ; the interrupts to the next phrase byte ($FF: no phrase)
@equ $7374 PhrasePtr 2 ; the phrase pair to send next

@isub $9BCB LD BC,Start
@isub $A425 LD BC,TitleText
@isub $A4CD LD BC,InstructionsText
@isub $AA9A LD BC,InstructionsText+102
@isub $A175 LD HL,$9808
@isub $A623 LD HL,$9F9E
@isub $9CF2 LD HL,PhraseTable-2
@isub $A38F LD HL,LiftPhrases-1
@isub $AAE6 LD HL,DeathPhrases-1
@isub $B14F LD HL,LevelPhrases-1
@isub $AABA LD HL,KeySet3-1
@isub $AB33 LD HL,KeyNames-6
@isub $A6E7 LD HL,LevelMaps-672
@isub $92F6 LD HL,HenSprites-2
@isub $AF35 LD HL,Screen-2
@isub $B0C3 LD HL,Screen-2
@isub $AA26 LD HL,Attributes+768
@isub $A751 LD HL,PlayerLives-1
@isub $A776 LD HL,PlayerLives-1
@isub $B115 LD DE,PlayerLives-1

@module tables ; The key sets, a leftover map row and the instructions page
@about The first bytes of the game block. Only KeySets and InstructionsText are read; the rest is what the author's assembler left (no build reads it).

$8214 b LeftoverMapRow 16 ; Leftover: a piece of a map row (a ladder 01 02, the cage's codes $A8 $A9)
> Never read or written (L1 of the eight builds: no access). The bytes look like a row of a level map (LevelMaps $B3B0 codes: 1 and 2 a ladder, $A8-$A9 the cage's top), left from an earlier layout of the image.

$8250 b KeySets 12 ; The three key sets: (mask, port row) for up, down, left, right, jump, jump
> SetupLevel $AE9C copies one set into KeyTable at every level start: type 1 ($8250, KeyType 6, the default) 2 W 9 0 and jump Z or M; type 2 ($825C, KeyType 5) 7 6 5 8 (the cursor joystick) and jump 4 or 9; type 3 ($8268, KeyType 3) the set RedefineKeys $AA49 writes (Q A O P, jump M or 1 in the image). A key is down when (IN (row x 256 + $FE) AND $1F) OR mask is not $1F. The editable form is src/res/text/KeySets.txt.
> Witness: SetupLevel's copy runs 35 times in the eight builds (tools/l1count.py $B0B8); tour-type2 reads $825C, tour-redefine writes $8268-$8271 (RedefineKeys clears ten bytes, RedefineOne writes five keys).
@res text/KeySets.bin
$825C KeySet2 ; type 2: the cursor keys
$8268 KeySet3 ; type 3: the set R redefines (its last pair, the second jump key, is never redefined)

$8274 s Zeros8274 ; 194 zeros
> Never read (L1: no access).

$8336 b MenuLeftover 30 ; Leftover: three menu lines with zeros for spaces
> Never read (L1: no access). Text of an earlier menu (src/res/text/MenuLeftover.txt); the game's menu texts are MenuTexts $ABF2.
@res text/MenuLeftover.bin

$8390 b InstructionsText 32 ; The instructions page: 11 rows of 32, the bottom row first
> InstructionsPage $A4C8 prints row k at character row 3 + 2k (from the bottom), so the page fills every other row of the screen; the editable form is src/res/text/InstructionsText.txt (top row first). RedefineKeys $AA49 and RedefineOne $AB19 write the new key names into row 3 of the page ($83F6, $83FB, $8400, $8405, $840A: up, down, left, right, jump), so the page shows the redefined set.
> Witness: InstructionsPage runs in c1, idle-1p, tour-type2 and tour-redefine; tour-redefine writes the five bytes.
@res text/InstructionsText.bin

@module graphics ; The character set, the HUD characters and the sprites
@about Every graphic is stored top row first. PrintChar $9C40 draws codes 0-$CB from CharacterSet (HudCharacters is its tail from code $9E), DrawSprite $9A4C the 17 frames of Sprites, DrawHen $929C the eight of HenSprites. The editable sheets are src/res/graphics/*.png and src/res/sprites/*.png.

$84F0 b CharacterSet 8 ; The character set, codes 0-$9D: the map cells, the font, the title logo
> Glyph = CharacterSet + 8 x code, top row first. Codes 0-5 are the map cells (empty, the ladder's two halves, the egg, the grain, the brick), $20-$7F the font ($41-$5A thin capitals, $61-$7A bold capitals, no lower case; $7E (R), $7F (C)), $80-$8E the quadrant blocks of the big CHUCKIE EGG of the title (TitleText uses $80-$8A), $8F-$96 the small A+F CHUCKIE EGG of the default names, $97-$9A the key names SPACE, CAPS SHIFT, SYMBOL SHIFT and ENTER, $9B-$9D LEVEL. Readers: PrintChar $9C40 (33 112 calls), DrawSprite $9A4C (the background cells), DrawHen $929C (the cells it erases, from $84F7, the last row), AddScore $A3A7 (the digits $30-$39 at $8670).
@res graphics/CharacterSet.bin

$89E0 b HudCharacters 8 ; Codes $9E-$CB: the HUD digits, the cage, the life icon, the cursor, the small A&F SOFTWARE
> The tail of the character set: $9E-$A7 the digits 0-9 of the HUD (CountDown $A1B8 reads them as HudCharacters + 8 x digit), $A8-$B5 the duck's cage, $B6 the life icon, $B7 the name entry's cursor, $B8-$CB the small A&F SOFTWARE. The digits are 7 rows under a blank top line, not larger than the font's $30-$39.
@res graphics/HudCharacters.bin

$8B50 s FillFF ; 672 bytes: 416 of $FF, then 256 of 0
> Never read (L1: no access): the size of one level map.

$8DF0 b Sprites 2 ; The 17 sprite frames of 16 x 16: Harry right 0-3, left 4-7, the duck 8-11, blank 12, climbing 13-16
> DrawSprite $9A4C copies frame A (Sprites + 32 x A, two bytes a row, top row first). Harry's frame is HarryFrame + HarryDir (0 right, 4 left, $0D climbing), the duck's 8 or 10 + DuckFrame (10-11 when Harry is left of it); frame 12 (blank) erases Harry when he lands on a lift and the duck before it moves. Harry walks with 0, 1, 0, 3: frame 2 is a byte-for-byte copy of 0; the left frames are the right ones mirrored bit for bit; Harry's frames leave row 0, row 15 and two columns each side blank, which is why a one-pixel move needs no erase. Witness: DrawSprite runs 134 270 times in the eight builds.
@res sprites/Sprites.bin

$9010 b HenSprites 2 ; The hens' eight frames of 16 x 16: walking 0, 1, 4, 5, climbing 2-3, pecking 6-7
> DrawHen $929C reads frame A - 1 from its last row up (HL = HenSprites - 2 + 32 x A). For a walk A is the state (1 left, 2 right) plus 4 when x AND 4 is set; for a climb 3, or 4 when y AND 4 is set; the pecks 7 and 8 are frames 6 (left) and 7 (right). Frames 0-1 fill columns 0-7, frames 4-5 (the next step of the same walk) columns 4-11: DrawHen writes whole bytes at x >> 3, so frames 4-5 are the walk pre-shifted by half a byte, the only stored shift in the game.
@res sprites/HenSprites.bin

$9110 b LeftoverSprite 14 ; Leftover: the first rows of a sprite frame
> Never read (L1: no access).

@module hens ; The hens: moving, eating grain, drawing, and the cell and screen addresses they use
@about MainLoop $9858 calls MoveHen once every HenDelay slow ticks; each call moves one of the five hen records at Hens. A hen walks along its platform, turns at an edge or a wall, takes a ladder at random, and eats the grain in front of it. DrawHen draws a hen and is where a hen kills Harry.

$911E c MoveHen ; Move the next hen one step
> Returns at once on levels 9-16 (Level 8-15). Otherwise it takes one random bit (RandomPtr steps through the ROM's first 256 bytes: C = 1 when bit 0 of the byte is 0), advances HenTurn (0-4) and takes that hen's record (x, y, state; x = $FF: no hen, return). It erases the hen (DrawHen with A = 0, which also tests Harry), then by the state:
> 7 or 8 (pecking): back to 1 or 2, the peck is erased and the hen drawn standing. 1 or 2 (walking left / right): when x AND 4 is 0 it first tries HenEatGrain, then turns (state 3 - state) when the next step x - 8 / x + 8 leaves the screen or the cell under it (y - 1) is neither a ladder nor a brick; then x moves 4 pixels and the hen is drawn; at a column where x AND 4 is set, and when the random bit allows, it goes onto a ladder: state 3 (down) when the cell 8 below is a ladder's left half, 4 (up) when the cell 16 above is (bit 1 of the random byte picks which it tests first).
> 3 or 4 (climbing down / up): when y AND 4 is 0 and the next cell is no ladder it turns (7 - state); y moves 4 pixels; at y AND 4 clear (the new y a multiple of 8) and the random bit it steps off onto a brick 8 left (state 1) or 16 right (state 2), the row 8 below.
> Inputs: the hen records. Outputs: the record moved; the screen. Side effects: RandomPtr, HenTurn; DrawHen may end the life (it unwinds the stack to $A656, the return of PlayLevel's CALL SetupLevel; SetupLevel enters MainLoop by JP $B12D). Witness: 38 158 calls in the eight builds (c1 801); turns $91A1 979, onto a ladder $91DB 324 and $91EF 228, off a ladder $924C 213 and $9261 307, meals $9281 82.
$9128 MoveHenRandom
$9138 MoveHenNext
$9142 MoveHenTurnSet
$916D MoveHenPeckErase
$9178 MoveHenWalk ; state 1-2: walking (3-8 go on at MoveHenClimb)
$918F MoveHenFloor
$91A1 MoveHenTurn ; state = 3 - state
$91A5 MoveHenStep ; x - 4 (state 1) or x + 4 (state 2), then draw
$91B0 MoveHenStepSet
$91CB MoveHenDown ; a ladder below: state 3
$91DB MoveHenSetDown
$91DF MoveHenUp ; a ladder above: state 4
$91EF MoveHenSetUp
$91F3 MoveHenClimb
$9201 MoveHenClimbTest
$920E MoveHenClimbStep ; y - 4 (state 3) or y + 4 (state 4), then draw
$921B MoveHenClimbSet
$923B MoveHenOffLeft ; a brick to the left: state 1
$924C MoveHenSetLeft
$9250 MoveHenOffRight ; a brick to the right: state 2
$9261 MoveHenSetRight

$9265 c HenEatGrain ; Eat the grain in front of a walking hen
> Input: HL the hen's state byte, E its x, D its y. The cell at (x + 8, y) for state 2 or (x - 8, y) for state 1 (MapCellAt $9E34): when it is grain (4) the cell becomes empty, the state becomes 7 or 8 (pecking) and the peck is drawn (8 pixels left for state 7); then it drops its own frame and MoveHen's (three POPs) and returns to MainLoop: the hen does not move this turn. Otherwise it returns with the registers kept.
> Witness: 6 746 calls, 82 meals ($9281); the grain is gone from LiveMap, so Harry can no longer take it.
> Known only from the code: when the peck's DrawHen finds Harry touching the hen, its six POPs are counted for MoveHen's stack, not this one's, so its RET takes the BC pushed at $9265 (B the state, C the random bit) as the return address. Only a left peck can get here (a right peck is drawn where MoveHen's erase has just tested the same box), so B = 1 and the RET goes to ROM $0100 or $0101. No build reached it. Tried on a clone (work/docs/ceC/heg.py, level 8, a hen at (160, 8) walking left, grain at (19, 1), Harry at (152, 23)): the PC goes to $0051, the ROM calculator, the RAM fill $11DE-$11ED, and the Spectrum resets to the copyright screen at frame 121; with Harry at 153 the normal kill and the death tune follow.
$9279 HenEatGrainTest
$9290 HenEatGrainPeck
$9298 HenEatGrainNone

$929C c DrawHen ; Test a hen against Harry, then draw or erase it
> Inputs: L the hen's x, H its y, A the frame (0: erase). First the box test against Harry: Harry's x within x - 7 .. x + 5 and his y within y + 1 .. y + $1C. A touch drops six words from the stack (DrawHen's four, its return and MoveHen's) and returns to $A656 in PlayLevel: the life ends ($92BC: c1 1, idle-1p 5, gameover-name 5, 11 in all).
> A > 0: the frame from HenSprites (see there) is ORed onto the screen, 16 lines from (x, y) up (ScreenAddr $9404; at x >= $F9 the DEC C at $9309 skips both bytes and only the attributes are set, never reached: a hen turns at $F8), and a block of attribute 5 (cyan) of 1-2 columns by 2-3 rows is set (AttrAddrHen $93DD). A = 0: the 2 x 3 map cells under the hen (1 x 3 at x >= $F8) are drawn again from LiveMap with their glyphs and CellAttributes. IX is HarryX at the end. Measured in levels-1-3 frames 600-900: a hen read blank by the beam in 7 of 44 steps.
> Witness: 44 867 calls.
$92AF DrawHenTestX
$92BE HenKill ; drop six words: back to $A656 in PlayLevel
$92C2 DrawHenFrame
$92D1 DrawHenWalkFrame
$92E1 DrawHenStepFrame
$92E7 DrawHenSprite
$9303 DrawHenScreen
$9308 DrawHenLine
$9317 DrawHenUp ; one screen line up
$932E DrawHenNext
$933F DrawHenAttrs
$9346 DrawHenAttrAt
$9349 DrawHenAttrRow
$934B DrawHenAttrCell
$935F EraseHen
$9369 EraseHenAt
$9380 EraseHenRow
$9385 EraseHenCell
$93A2 EraseHenGlyph
$93BF EraseHenNextRow

$93DD c AttrAddrHen ; HL = the attribute address of pixel (L, H)
> Input: L = x, H = y. Output: HL = $5800 + x / 8 + 32 x ((191 - y) / 8). AF and DE kept. Witness: 44 856 calls (DrawHen). The same code is CellAttrAddr $9584 (into DE) and SpriteAttrAddr $9BDE.

$93FE c MapCellAddrKeepA ; HL = the map cell address of (L, H), A kept
> MapCellAt $9E34 with AF saved: HL = the cell's address in LiveMap. Witness: 22 474 calls (EraseHen).

$9404 c ScreenAddr ; HL = the screen address of pixel (L, H)
> Input: L = x, H = y (0 at the bottom). Output: HL = the display file byte of that pixel row (the third from y / 64, the character row from y AND $38, the line from (y AND 7) XOR 7). AF, BC and DE kept. Witness: 44 856 calls (DrawHen).
$9418 ScreenAddrMiddle
$9419 ScreenAddrRow

$9438 c MapCellPeek ; A = the map cell at (L, H), HL kept
> MapCellAt $9E34 with HL saved. Witness: 19 822 calls (MoveHen's floor and ladder tests).

$943E b LeftoverCode943E 16 ; Leftover: copies of code bytes from an earlier assembly
> Never read (L1: no access). F1 C9 E5 CD 34 9E E1 C9 is the end of ScreenAddr and MapCellPeek ($9436-$943D), the rest the middle of ScreenAddr ($940C-$9421), shifted by an earlier layout.

$945B b HenTable 21 ; The hens of levels 1-8: a count, then up to five hen records
> SetupLevel $AE9C reads the row at $945B + 21 x ((Level AND 7) + 1), so row 0 here ($945B) is never read: level 1's row is $9470. The first byte is the number of bytes to copy into Hens (8 on level 1, 12 on 2-3, 16 on 4-6, 12 on 7-8: two to four hens), then the records (x, y, state, spare). Levels 9-16 copy none, 17-24 the table again, 25 and up all 20 bytes (five hens). The editable form is src/res/tables/HenTable.csv.
> Witness: SetupLevel's copy at $AFA4: 35 levels in the eight builds.
@res tables/HenTable.bin

$9518 s Zeros9518 ; 32 zeros
> Never read (L1: no access).

@module render ; The attributes under a sprite and the map cell address
@about PaintCells restores the map's colours where a sprite was; MapCellAddr turns a pixel position into a LiveMap address.

$9538 c PaintCells ; Paint the attributes of the 3 x 3 map cells at (L, H)
> Input: L = x, H = y of a sprite. From the cell under (x, y) down, three rows of three cells (two columns at x >= $F1, as DrawSprite; two rows only at y < $11, with no y AND 7 test) get their attribute from CellAttributes (code 9 and up: 6). Only the attributes are painted: DrawSprite $9A4C redraws the pixels with the background. Registers kept.
> Callers: MainLoop before Harry moves, JumpStep before each step, JumpFall $A2BE before each fall step, MoveDuck before the duck moves. Witness: 147 583 calls.
$9544 PaintCellsRows
$954C PaintCellsStart
$9552 PaintCellsRow
$9555 PaintCellsCell
$955E PaintCellsAttr
$9566 PaintCellsSet

$9584 c CellAttrAddr ; DE = the attribute address of pixel (L, H)
> As AttrAddrHen $93DD, the result in DE. Witness: 147 583 calls (PaintCells).

$95A6 c MapCellAddr ; HL = the LiveMap address of the cell at pixel (L, H)
> Output: HL = LiveMap + x / 8 + 4 x (y AND $F8): row y / 8 from the bottom, 32 cells a row. Witness: 147 583 calls (PaintCells).

$95C5 s Zeros95C5 ; 107 zeros
> Never read (L1: no access).

@module screens ; The title page, the HUD text, the lifts, the high score table and the cell colours
@about Data the menu and the level set-up print or copy; the editable forms are under src/res/text and src/res/tables.

$9630 b TitleText 14 ; The title page's left half: 22 rows of 14 codes, the bottom row first
> TitlePage $A420 prints row k at character row 2 + k from the bottom, columns 0-13; codes $80-$8A are the big CHUCKIE EGG (its only codes from $80 up; the small A+F CHUCKIE EGG $8F-$96 is in HiScoreTable). The editable form is src/res/text/TitleText.txt (top row first). Witness: TitlePage runs 4 times in the eight builds.
@res text/TitleText.bin

$9764 b HudText 35 ; The HUD: the SCORE label for the top row, 32 codes for the third
> SetupLevel $AE9C prints the first three (SCORE, codes $0B-$0D) at character row 23 (the top), the 32 at row 21: PLAYER ($0E-$11), LEVEL ($9B-$9D), BONUS ($1B-$1D) and TIME ($12-$14), each with its digits. It writes the digits first: $976B the player, $9772-$9773 the level, $977A the bonus's thousands, $9784 the time's hundreds (codes $9E + digit, HudCharacters); the image holds level 1's.
@res text/HudText.bin
$976B HudPlayer ; the player's digit
$9772 HudLevel ; the level's two digits
$977A HudBonus ; the bonus's thousands digit
$9784 HudTime ; the time's hundreds digit

$9787 b LiftTable 4 ; The lifts: the record in play, then one a level (1-8)
> A record is the screen address of the platform's start (two bytes), the lift's x ($FF: no lift) and its height count at the start (3). SetupLevel $AE9C copies level (Level AND 7) + 1's record over the first one and into Lift1; MoveLifts $A014 restarts a platform from the first one when it reaches the top. Lifts on levels 3-7 (x $40, $90, $C8, $78, $F0), none on 1, 2 and 8. The editable form is src/res/tables/LiftTable.csv. Witness: the restarts $A02E (164) and $A05C (167) in levels-1-3, gameover-name and levels-1-9.
@res tables/LiftTable.bin

$97AB b Leftover97AB 4 ; Leftover bytes
> Never read (L1: no access).

$97AF b HiScoreTable 16 ; The ten best scores: ten name bytes and six digits each, the best first
> DrawHiScores $ABAD prints the table; EnterHiScore $A80C compares a score with each entry's digits ($97B9 + 16 k), shifts the lower entries down and writes the new one. The digits are ASCII ($30-$39), as GameOver $A7BC makes the scores. The editable form is src/res/text/HiScoreTable.txt. Witness: gameover-name writes one entry.
@res text/HiScoreTable.bin

$984F b CellAttributes 9 ; The attribute of map cell codes 0-8
> PaintCells $9538, EraseHen and SetupLevel $AE9C read CellAttributes + code (codes 9 and up take 6, yellow): empty 6, the ladder 3 and 3 (magenta), the egg 7, the grain 3, the brick 4 (green), then 6, 7, 7. The editable form is src/res/tables/CellAttributes.csv.
@res tables/CellAttributes.bin

@module mainloop ; The main loop and the pickup of eggs and grain
@about MainLoop is entered by SetupLevel's JP at $B12D and left only by a RET (or by a routine that unwinds the stack to it): the RET returns to $A656 in PlayLevel, after CALL SetupLevel. Each pass checks ERR_SP, plays the pickup sound and runs the jump; every 130th pass (PassCounter) the slow tick runs everything else.

$9858 c MainLoop ; One pass of the game: the jump every pass, the rest every 130th pass
> 1. ERR_SP must be 1 (tape block 3): otherwise the game hangs at $985E. 2. The pickup sound: every 16 passes, while SoundSweep is not 0, it counts down and every fourth count beeps (H = (SoundSweep AND $1F) + 6, two cycles). 3. While JumpState is not 0: a click whose pitch follows HarryY on the pass before the slow tick, JumpStep $A21C, and after a vertical step the hens are tested against Harry (HenTouches $9E66): a touch returns (the life ends).
> 4. PassCounter counts 130 passes; then the slow tick: CAPS SHIFT + H holds the game until S, CAPS SHIFT + A aborts to Start $A410; the bonus every 50 ticks (CountDown B = 0), the duck every 12 (MoveDuck $A0C8), the lifts every 2 (MoveLifts $A014; Harry on a lift rises one pixel and dies at y $A5), the pickup (TakeEggOrGrain $99DF), the time every 10 with a tick (CountDown B = 1), one hen every 3 ticks (2 from level 33; MoveHen $911E), PaintCells at Harry.
> 5. Then Harry: on foot, a jump key starts a jump (JumpState 2, JumpCount $8C, JumpDy 1, OnLift 0; the direction from left / right, else straight up); otherwise LeaveLadder $9F60, WalkHarry $9D08 unless climbing, FallOffEdge $B34C unless on a lift, and ClimbLadder $9E98 (also in the air: a jump catches a ladder).
> Witness: 14 873 212 passes in the eight builds, 113 934 slow ticks ($99D9); 477 jumps started ($9975); 920 lift steps with Harry on board ($991E). The hold and abort keys ($98C8-$98E5): hold-abort, HOLD entered at frame 1100 T 54 699 and left at 1300 T 305, ABORT to Start $A410 at 1400 T 29 350. Known only from the code: the faster hens ($9944).
