@res text/SourceLeftoverB167.bin

$B200 s VectorTable ; The IM 2 vector table: 263 bytes of $9C
> I = $B2 (Start): an interrupt with $FF on the bus reads $B2FF-$B300, $9C9C, PhraseVector. Witness: only $B2FF-$B300 are read (243 240 reads).

$B307 b SourceLeftoverB307 16 ; Leftover: the author's assembler source
> Never read (L1: no access); src/res/text/SourceLeftoverB307.txt.
@res text/SourceLeftoverB307.bin

$B34C c FallOffEdge ; Start a fall when Harry walks off a platform's edge
> Only when x AND 7 is not 0. The cell under his feet (MapCellAt - $3F): a brick or more, or a ladder, keeps him. Else (empty, an egg, grain) JumpState 1, JumpDx his direction, JumpCount 4: he drifts four slow ticks, then falls (JumpStep $A21C). MainLoop calls it on foot when not on a lift ($99D6).
> Witness: 98 837 calls, 63 falls ($B368). This routine lies inside the leftover text: the code runs at $911E-$B15E and $B34C-$B380.
$B368 FallOffEdgeStart
$B377 FallOffEdgeDir

$B381 b SourceLeftoverB381 16 ; Leftover: the author's assembler source
> Never read (L1: no access); src/res/text/SourceLeftoverB381.txt.
@res text/SourceLeftoverB381.bin

$B3B0 b LevelMaps 32 ; The eight level maps of 21 rows of 32 cells, the bottom row first: level 1
> StartGame copies level 1 into every LiveMap slot, PlayLevel the next level's (LevelMaps + 672 x (Level AND 7)) into the map in play: levels 9-16 repeat 1-8, and so on. Codes: 0 empty, 1 and 2 a ladder, 3 an egg, 4 grain, 5 a brick, $A8-$B5 the cage. The editable forms are src/res/maps/Level1.txt .. Level8.txt (top row first), the figures docs/img/maps.
@res maps/Level1.bin
